[00:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'All right, YouTube. What is good? It\'s your boy Rebel back with another video. And today, we are going to be taking a look at Mage Flow. Mage Flow is a compact 4 billion scale generative stack for efficient textto image generation and instruction based image editing. The'

[00:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stack is built from two codeesign components. Mage VAE, a lightweight highfidelity latent tokenizer and a native resolution multimodel diffusion transformer trained with rectified flow'

[00:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'matching. Now on release there were four models and variations. So Microsoft did however take down the model from hugging face but the comfy or teams version is still up in BF-16 format with int8'

[00:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'combat versions as well for lower VRAM cost compute as the int8 is only 4 GB which should fit on most cards. I will also link a guff format for the extremely low VRAM. During testing for'

[00:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this model I realized a lot of issues just in the base model and turbo model. A lot of the photorealistic outputs that I was trying to achieve had, you know, hallucinations on the face or hands.'

[01:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There was a lot of artifacting and just generalized issues throughout most of the generations in my testing. So, this would have been a singular output from mage on its own. This is a base model generation. What I did was added a And'

[01:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what I did was add a Korea 2 turbo pass at four steps with a D noiseis of.35 to refine and clean up the image. As you can see, the eyes are fixed. The'

[01:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'keyboard is fixed. All of the minor details on the woman are corrected. It is more sharpened and cleaner of a result. So, I built this workflow off of the mage flow workflow that is native in'

[01:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the comfy templates. Now, as all four of these templates are available for you guys if you would like to check out the other variations of the model. Today, we will not be looking at the edit or the turbo. We will just be looking at the'

[02:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mage flow base model as the base model tends to do better than the distillation method that provides a very strict aesthetic in the turbo models. So, we will be looking at the base model. So I have developed this workflow off of the'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'base workflow in the templates for mage flow. What it is is just the regular simple template workflow with a text input node running to both the positive prompting for mage and ka with some'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clean VRAM and clear cache nodes. Those are available in the comfy manager under the easy use node set. So you can just go to the comfy manager, download the comfy UI easy use nodes and you\'ll have'

[02:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these. And then inside the Create 2 refinement subgraph, we have a Laura that is bypassed. And we also have the conditioning rebalancing node for those who want to do anything outside of the'

[02:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'filter. And that pretty much does account for the workflow. You just need to make sure that you activate all of your models in both subgraphs. And if you would like to play around with the steps or D noiseis, it is right here in'

[03:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Crea 2 Turbo Refiner subgraph. So if you need to adjust anything there or change your Laura and strength values, you can do that here. Other than that, that does account for the workflow. But I would like to really quickly just'

[03:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'explain something to you guys. You can do this at any point that you choose. You do not need to wait for, you know, a creator workflow to do this. as inside your subgraph here for creat 2 turbo there is just a simple VAE encode node'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and what this VAE encode node does is it takes the finished image from the mage flow workflow section and it passes it into this encoder with the crea 2 encoder so it can pull the latent data'

[03:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and throw it to the k sampler. So essentially, if you wanted to, you know, mix and match any two models, all you need to do is connect your output from the save image and pass it into the VAE encode of your second workflow. So you'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would essentially just like copy this whole workflow, bring it into another workflow, and just throw all of your information into the VAE encode. And then you don\'t have to worry about your resolution or anything like that with'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this second refinement pass as it already has the information from the latent data that we just passed from the first model which would be mage flow in this case. So remember first model pass the save image data into a VAE encode'

[04:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'node run the latent into your second kampler and workflow and you have a dual pass workflow to clean up or change anything about your first image that you didn\'t like or just wanted to add to. So, I do have some examples for you guys'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'today and we will be taking a look at those. Now, back to our first example that we had. Here we have the woman playing at her gaming PC. Now, as you can see, the eyes and overall detail composition is just very weak. There\'s a'

